WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.901
If you die without a will,

2
00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:08.100
you don't get a say in who receives your things.

3
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.690
Every state has a default rulebook,

4
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.004
called intestacy.

5
00:00:12.004 --> 00:00:13.135
In most states,

6
00:00:13.135 --> 00:00:17.100
it generally starts with your spouse and children.

7
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.456
With no spouse or children,

8
00:00:19.456 --> 00:00:21.088
it moves to parents,

9
00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:25.100
then siblings, then more distant relatives.

10
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.959
An unmarried partner,

11
00:00:26.959 --> 00:00:28.217
a close friend,

12
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:30.909
or a charity usually gets nothing.

13
00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:31.992
And a judge,

14
00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:36.600
not you, may decide who raises your minor children.

15
00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:40.186
The court appoints someone to handle things.

16
00:00:40.186 --> 00:00:43.145
That process can take months.

17
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.908
A will, plus powers of attorney,

18
00:00:45.908 --> 00:00:47.884
lets you choose instead.

19
00:00:47.884 --> 00:00:51.100
It usually takes a short meeting.

20
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.572
Not sure what you need?

21
00:00:53.572 --> 00:00:57.180
Take our three-minute plan finder.
